.TH KTON 1 "2026-07-07" "kton v0" "kton manual"
.SH NAME
kton \- the cockpit that conducts plankton + nekton (network, anchoring, pinning)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kton
.I command
[\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kton
orchestrates
.BR plankton (1)
and
.BR nekton (1)
but \fBreimplements nothing\fR - every operation is a call into a kernel. Delete kton and each
operation is still runnable directly.
.PP
It exists to hold the surface deliberately kept OUT of the kernels so they stay minimal and
WebAssembly-compilable: the \fBnetwork\fR (serving a port, mirroring a URL peer), the
\fBtransparency log\fR (Rekor anchoring), and optional \fBbyte pinning\fR. Pure, local
overlay-by-hash federation stays in the kernels (\fBplankton mirror\fR / \fBnekton mirror\fR on a
directory); kton adds the network peer. Like the kernels, kton never executes your programs.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B kton serve plankton [\fIaddr\fR]
Serve the plankton federation API over HTTP (default :8787).
.TP
.B kton serve nekton [\fIaddr\fR]
Serve the nekton federation API over HTTP (default :8788).
.TP
.B kton mirror plankton \fIpeer\fR [--pin]
Pull + persist a peer plankton registry. \fIpeer\fR is a URL (needs a running \fBkton serve\fR) or
a local registry directory (read directly, no port). \fB--pin\fR (URL peer only) also fetches and
re-serves the verified bytes.
.TP
.B kton mirror nekton \fIpeer\fR
Pull + persist a peer nekton registry (URL or local directory).
.TP
.B kton anchor \fIenvelope.dsse.json\fR \fIpubkey.pub\fR|\fIhex\fR
Anchor a signed record in the Rekor transparency log (Sigstore) and verify the inclusion proof at
anchor time. NOTE: the proof is printed to stdout, not (yet) embedded in the record, and there is no
offline re-verification of a saved proof - see the spec's long-term-verifiability clause. The
public key may be a .pub file path or the hex string.
.TP
.B kton pin \fIfile\fR
Pin a file's bytes into the plankton blob store (optional; the kernel stores no bytes).
.TP
.B kton blob \fIsha256:...\fR
Is this content pinned locally?
.TP
.B kton fetch \fIsha256:...\fR
Resolve content to its bytes via signed nekton \fBlocated-at\fR claims (predicate
\fBdcat:downloadURL\fR): dereference each suggested URI, verify the SHA-256, and pin. Fails if no
signed location claim exists for the hash. The kernels never resolve URIs - this is a cockpit job.
.TP
.B kton man
Print this manual page (roff source; pipe to \fBman -l -\fR to render). Embedded in the binary.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PLANKTON_DIR
plankton registry directory (default ./plankton-data).
.TP
.B NEKTON_DIR
nekton registry directory (default ./nekton-data).
.SH EXAMPLES
Share one session's results with another over the network:
.RS
.nf

  # session A
  PLANKTON_DIR=A kton serve plankton :8787
  # session B
  PLANKTON_DIR=B kton mirror plankton http://localhost:8787
.fi
.RE
.PP
Or, with no server at all, mirror a local directory with the kernel:
.RS
.nf

  PLANKTON_DIR=B plankton mirror ../A/plankton-data
.fi
.RE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR plankton (1),
.BR nekton (1)
